  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "Parts are the same as step 1; nothing added or dropped.",
   "Circuit: D2 -> green wire -> 220 ohm resistor -> LED anode; LED cathode -> black wire -> GND, as in the image and schematic.",
   "Breadboard holes use the catalogue naming (top half = 't', rows a-e). Resistor spans columns 3 and 6, LED anode (the bent, longer leg) is in column 6 and cathode in column 8, all in the same half. Each wire shares a column strip with its component leg.",
   "The MKR WiFi 1010 board is placed beside the breadboard, not on it, and is not drawn as plugged into it; the wires go to its header pins D2 and GND.",
   "The tutorial code reads analog pin A1 with nothing connected, so no part is wired to A1.",
   "The 220 ohm resistor sits on the LED anode side, as in the schematic. The LED draws about 20 mA, within the board's limit of 7 mA per pin in the catalogue only if the current is lower: (3.3 V - 2.0 V) / 220 ohm is about 6 mA, which fits."
  ]
 },
